 "about": [
  "Manx is a Gaelic language, a close cousin of Irish and Scottish Gaelic, spoken on the Isle of Man.",
  "Ned Maddrell, the last native speaker, died in 1974. Learners never let it go.",
  "Today children can go to school in Manx at the Bunscoill Ghaelgagh in St John's."
 ],
